            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I served this for a baby shower with cinnamon pita chips and it was a huge hit. The smaller you chop up the fruit the better and I drained a little of the juice off before serving just so it was easier to eat. I'll definitely make this again!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Renee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "So yummy! I served it with cinnamon/sugar pita chips and it was devoured! I had a little bit leftover the next day and threw it in my blender with some vanilla yogurt and ice to make one of the best smoothies I've ever tasted!",
            "datePublished": "2009-02-09T07:34:26.667Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TwoSweetPickles"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yum! I wanted to serve this as a savory salsa, so I added a jalapeno. I used the liquid to marinate chicken breasts and grilled them, then topped with the salsa. Excellent and I'll use this often when mangos are available.",
            "datePublished": "2010-05-01T19:52:21.077Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "stonercy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have made this twice since I found the recipe! Yummm! The first time I nixed the orange juice and used a walnut/raspberry vinegrette instead of the balsamic vinegar. I liked the added sweetness. The second time I made it exactly like the recipe and didn't care for the extra liquid. In the future will half the liquid for the recipe. Great with grahm crackers!",
            "datePublished": "2011-03-27T11:32:09.983Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "bbenso1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this yesterday for a family bbq and everyone loved it! I halved the recipe, but I shouldn't of. It was gone in a flash! I did add about 1/2 a jalapeno, diced and some chopped cilantro as suggested by another reviewer. Fantastic summer recipe, I will definitely make this again.",
            "datePublished": "2008-06-22T13:47:13.557Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "elizabethcostello"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It 'needs something' and I think that something is either buttloads of fresh good salt (no iodized), chilli or a green object like spring onion, parsley or coriander (cilantro) or all of the above. It needs to be 'more'. I had all the ingredients on hand and added parsley, pink salt, and twice the balsamic it asked for as well as some green onion and that really seemed to bring that flavour together a bit better. I used it to top pasta because I didn't have anything else and was hungry for this. It hit the spot, either way.",
            "datePublished": "2012-11-08T17:47:02.650Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "the taste tester"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this with my closest friend...just for fun because we both love to cook. We squeezed all the jucies by hand, and it was AMAZING! We found that apple cinnamon chips (flat earth brand) tasted the best and we perffered it unchilled, left it a little more tangy. So if you want to pucker and smile at the same time, this is what you want! Perfect summer recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2008-07-03T07:58:00.527Z"
          },
          {
